{#- Sponsor page: the three ways in, as photo cards in their own pastel. script.js weaves the snake
    through them, under the first, over the middle one and under the last. No blank lines: Markdown includes this -#}
<div class="doors" data-doors>
  <svg class="snake doors-snake" aria-hidden="true"></svg>
  <div class="doors-row">
    <article class="door door-blue" data-reveal>
      {% photo "photos/bof.jpg", "A PyDelhi meetup in a company meeting room, a speaker at the screen", "(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 360px", { class: "door-img", loading: "lazy" } %}
      <span class="door-tag"><i class="ph ph-door-open"></i> Host</span>
      <h3>The room</h3>
      <p>Seats for a full room, a projector or screen, a mic and Wi-Fi, and a way in for visitors on a Saturday.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="door door-yellow" data-reveal style="--d:120ms">
      {% photo "blog/8-july-2018-lunch.jpg", "Attendees eating lunch together at a long table during a PyDelhi meetup", "(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 360px", { class: "door-img", loading: "lazy" } %}
      <span class="door-tag"><i class="ph ph-coffee"></i> Feed</span>
      <h3>Food and chai</h3>
      <p>The break is where people meet, ask follow-up questions and find collaborators. Keep it going.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="door door-green" data-reveal style="--d:240ms">
      {% photo "photos/aiohttp-talk.jpeg", "A speaker presenting a talk on aiohttp at a PyDelhi meetup", "(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 360px", { class: "door-img", loading: "lazy" } %}
      <span class="door-tag"><i class="ph ph-hand-coins"></i> Fund</span>
      <h3>Recordings and travel</h3>
      <p>Recording talks for YouTube, swag for speakers, and travel for speakers who come from out of town.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</div>
